Z||000000||Beaverman||09-03-2001||10:47 PM||||I have an 87 Fiero GT.  It recently Stalled/sputtered on the highway coming home from work.  I finally got it towed back home and replaced the EGR, Ignition Module, O2 Sensor using parts from my parts car.  It seems to get ANNOYINGLY more hot then it used to get.  I thought i had the problem fixed today after retiming it, but 1 mile from my apartment it sputtered then died going 45 miles an hour.  Pulled to the side and it started up, put it in drive and pushed down on the gas and got no power then it got power then lost power.  I'm lost on what to do with it so any help would be appreciated.  I've also replaced the spark plugs and put Spiral Core High Heat plug wires on it.  And when it sputters/Dies/Loses power sometimes the check engine light comes on and sometimes it doesn't.  Is there any way to check my trouble codes without having to have a GM Diag tool?  Thanks for help.  87 2.8 V6.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ed||09-03-2001||10:52 PM||||Another possibility is your catalytic convertor.<P>You can check your codes by using a paper clip to short out your A and B terminals in your diagnostic connection under your cigarette lighter panel.  See archives. ||||reg||1
